# Docker matches these from the context root — a bare name like `__pycache__`
# excludes only the top-level one and lets nested caches through, which is how
# .pyc files carrying an absolute host path (a maintainer's home directory) once
# ended up inside a locally built image. Every entry is therefore recursive.
.git
.github
!.github/workflows/build-and-publish.yml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
keys.env
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.privacy-deny.local
# docs/ (the README screenshot) stays in the build context: the test stage asserts the
# README's links resolve, and the runtime stage never copies it, so it cannot ship.
